# JetBrains HTTP Client format: talk to the bookstore assistant, a chat that answers questions about the catalogue with the help of read-only tools.
# The endpoint is POST /assistant/chat. The body holds a conversationId (a UUID) and a message. A good answer is 200 with the same conversationId and the reply.
# The conversationId in these requests is {{$uuid}}, a new UUID for every send, so each request starts a new conversation. To continue a conversation, put the conversationId of an earlier answer into the next body.
# Run mode: the answer depends on the API key. When the bookstore was started without the BOOKSTORE_AI_API_KEY environment variable it runs in offline mode and answers 503 with the error code assistant-offline. With the key set when the bookstore starts, the assistant answers 200.
# Failed model call: with the key set, a failed model call (wrong key, spend or rate limit at Anthropic, timeout) answers 503 with the error code assistant-unavailable.
# Rate limit: with the key set, the bookstore passes at most 20 chat requests per minute. The 21st request within a minute is refused with 429 Too Many Requests, a problem answer without an error code, and the model is not called. In offline mode the offline answer comes first, so 429 does not appear.
# A message is limited to 1000 characters. A longer message is refused with 400 and the error code validation-failed.
# Each request has a line "Expected status:" in its comment. A label in parentheses names the run mode that the status belongs to.

# Ask for a recommendation.
# Expected status: 200 (api key set); 503 (no api key).
POST http://localhost:8080/assistant/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, application/problem+json

{
  "conversationId": "{{$uuid}}",
  "message": "Recommend two science fiction books under 15 euro"
}

###

# Ask whether a book is in stock. The assistant looks it up with its tools, so the answer names a title that the catalogue holds.
# Expected status: 200 (api key set); 503 (no api key).
POST http://localhost:8080/assistant/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, application/problem+json

{
  "conversationId": "{{$uuid}}",
  "message": "Is Treasure Island in stock?"
}

###

# Send a message that is only blank. The check of the body comes first, so the answer is 400 with the error code validation-failed in both run modes.
# Expected status: 400.
POST http://localhost:8080/assistant/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, application/problem+json

{
  "conversationId": "{{$uuid}}",
  "message": "   "
}

###

# Send a message without a conversationId. The answer is 400 with the error code validation-failed in both run modes.
# Expected status: 400.
POST http://localhost:8080/assistant/chat
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, application/problem+json

{
  "message": "Hello"
}
